{
  "abstract": "Every finite simple graph without an isolated edge has edge weights in {1,...,5} such that adjacent vertices have different weighted degrees (Kalkowski, Karoński and Pfender 2010). The {1,...,30} bound of Addario-Berry et al. (2007) follows as a corollary. The 1-2-3 conjecture itself (Karoński, Łuczak and Thomason 2004), with weights {1, 2, 3}, was later proved by Keusch (2024); this entry formalizes the earlier {1,...,5} theorem, not Keusch's proof.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Wentao Li"
    }
  ],
